#!/usr/bin/env python3
# A PYTHON LAUNCHER IS INVISIBLE TO A SHELL COMMAND-POSITION PARSER: mesh-doctor's call corpus
# reads shell command position, and `LETTER = "mesh-job-letter"` -> subprocess.run([LETTER, ...])
# is a MENTION there, never a launch — so every tool this file dispatches reads as an orphan and
# is a candidate for deletion on that verdict. The declaration sits on the LAUNCHER, never on the
# launched tool, so it is not a self-exemption.
# launches: mesh-hh-drive mesh-job-letter mesh-job-answers mesh-tg
"""mesh-job-apply — rank the board, apply to the top N on hh, prove each one landed.

  mesh-job-apply [--top N] [--dry] [--tg] [--json]
  mesh-job-apply --reasons                      -> что держит каждую строку в needs-human
  mesh-job-apply --backfill-reasons [--dry]     -> разово: токен причины строкам без колонки
  mesh-job-apply --reopen [--harvest] [--dry]   -> вернуть в seen то, чья причина снята
  mesh-job-apply --reconcile [--dry]            -> сверить доску со списком откликов hh
  mesh-job-apply --settle [--dry]               -> досудить строки, исчерпавшие попытки
  mesh-job-apply --fix-profile [--dry]          -> видимость резюме -> самый широкий доступный
  mesh-job-apply --test

# reflex-cadence: 23 7 * * *
# reflex-args: --tg

Sends real applications under the operator's own name, so every guard here is load-bearing:

* **Gate.** Refuses unless `MESH_JOB_AUTOAPPLY=on` is exported (`~/.mesh/nodes`). A tool that
  sends mail as a human must not be armed by merely existing on a node.
* **Daily cap.** `MESH_JOB_DAILY_CAP` (default 5) counted from board rows already marked sent
  TODAY, so a crash-loop or a double-wired cron cannot carpet-bomb employers.
* **Letters are assembled, never generated** (`mesh-job-letter`) — his own approved paragraphs
  only. A vacancy the block set cannot speak to is SKIPPED, not sent a generic letter.
* **His employment history is a ban list, and it is filled BEFORE the run.** `sync_blacklist()`
  reads the employers out of his own CV files at the top of every run and writes them into
  `job/blacklist.txt` as `former:` lines — a kind distinct from `dedup:`, because one is etiquette
  and the other is his life. Nothing in the scoring knew he had ever had a job until 2026-08-21,
  when the ranker put Foxible (dispute, `job/foxible-dispute-2026-08-14.md`) into a batch and what
  stopped it was a page that failed to load. `allow: <name>` is his override and survives a sync.
* **A letter under `sent/` means hh CONFIRMED the application.** Unconfirmed letters go to
  `job/unconfirmed/UNCONFIRMED-*.md`. The file used to be written off the click's own verdict,
  one pass before the verifier that could still flip the row.
* **Screening forms are ANSWERED, from his own bank, and never invented.** hh routes some
  responses through employer questions (Ozon does). This used to stop the lane: the tool answered
  nothing, marked `needs-human`, and the doctrine here read "ticking an unread question on someone's
  behalf is never worth automating". The operator revoked that hand-back twice — 2026-08-25 «все
  needs-human вы можете смело заполнять за меня, включая тесты, опросники» and 2026-08-28 «у вас
  есть все чтобы доводить до интервью самим». What made the old sentence true was UNREAD, not
  ANSWERED: the honest boundary is not who ticks the box, it is whether the answer is HIS. So the
  questions are harvested off the page (`--reopen --harvest`), matched against `job/answers.tsv` —
  his own approved facts — and only a question the bank cannot cover is queued for him. An
  ANSWERED-FROM-HIS-BANK question is our work; an INVENTED one is still never worth automating,
  and nothing here invents.
* **`needs-human` carries WHY, in column 7, and the WHY is removable.** The state alone was a
  one-way door: nine rows sat in it with the cause only in prose, so nothing could ask "is the
  cause gone yet?" and no hand but the operator's could ever re-open one. Each token names WHO
  clears it — `questions` the answer bank, `retry` time, `profile` US (`--fix-profile` edits the
  visibility setting in his hh account), `letter` US (we write the missing paragraph into
  `letter-blocks.md` from his own CV), `form` the code, and `captcha` — the ONE token left that
  genuinely waits on a human, which no site in this lane has yet minted. `--reopen` re-opens
  exactly the rows whose clearer has acted. A cause
  that cannot be placed in the window where it would be judged is HELD, never cleared: an origin
  with no harvested questions is formally "covered by the bank" and re-opening on that would be a
  positive verdict issued by a hand that measured nothing.
* **The artifact is the negotiations list, not the click.** hh's own profile-completion modal
  swallows clicks while reporting success — a first hand-run looked green through the entire
  cover-letter step with no application filed. So a row flips to `sent` only after the vacancy id
  appears in hh.ru/applicant/negotiations.

Ranking is deterministic: salary floor, keyword weight against his profile, seniority match,
penalty for a missing salary. Nothing here asks a model what a good job is.
"""
import argparse, collections, fcntl, json, os, pathlib, re, shutil, subprocess, sys, tempfile, time
import types

import signal

# SIGTERM MUST UNWIND, or every `finally` below is decorative. Python's DEFAULT SIGTERM disposition
# terminates the interpreter WITHOUT running finally blocks, TemporaryDirectory.__exit__ or atexit,
# so a correct-looking cleanup never executes. The signal is routine here, not hypothetical: GNU
# `timeout` without --foreground puts its child in its OWN PROCESS GROUP and signals the GROUP, so
# every timeout-wrapped call site -- mesh-doctor's hourly --test sweep, mesh-autowire's `timeout 30`
# -- delivers TERM to this process. That is how 950MB of stranded snapshots filled phaedra's /tmp on
# 2026-08-16 with a `finally: rmtree` sitting right there in the source (first fixed in mesh-spend,
# d2fd7c9b). sys.exit() from a handler raises SystemExit in the MAIN THREAD, which is what makes
# try/finally unwind. SIGKILL stays uncatchable -- that half is mesh-tmp-guard's sweep, never this.
for _sig in (signal.SIGTERM, signal.SIGHUP):
    signal.signal(_sig, lambda _s, _f: sys.exit(128 + _s))


